[CHANGE] benchmark_1/parts/dag_engine/tests/dag_engine_impl_test.py: Implemented comprehensive test suite for DAG, WaveScheduler, and DAGRunner covering all low-level spec contracts. Tests include: DAG operations (add_node, add_edge, remove_node, has_node, get_node, get_dependencies, get_dependents, all_nodes), validation (acyclicity, missing deps), topological sort (priority/tie-breaking, cycle detection), roots/leaves queries, critical path computation, WaveScheduler (next_wave, mark_running, mark_succeeded, mark_failed with FAIL_FAST/SKIP_DOWNSTREAM/CONTINUE_ON_ERROR policies, is_finished, get_state, get_all_states), and DAGRunner (run execution, cancel, DAGRunReport structure verification). All tests use lifecycle-registered isolated registries with enter_phase scopes.
[CHANGE] benchmark_1/parts/dag_engine/lib/dag_engine.py: Implemented lib/dag_engine.py: interface module with data types (DAGError, CycleError, NodeNotFoundError, NodeExecutionError, DAGTimeoutError, DAGCancelledError), enums (NodeState, FailurePolicy), value types (NodeDefinition, NodeResult, DAGRunReport), and service protocols (DAG, WaveScheduler, DAGRunner) as system-tier singletons inheriting Singleton[SystemTier] and Protocol.
[CHANGE] benchmark_1/parts/dag_engine/lib/dag_engine_impl.py: Implemented lib/dag_engine_impl.py: concrete DAG, WaveScheduler, and DAGRunner singletons with full graph operations (add/remove nodes/edges, validation, topological sort, critical path), wave-based scheduling with failure policies (FAIL_FAST, SKIP_DOWNSTREAM, CONTINUE_ON_ERROR), concurrent execution with retry logic and timeout/cancellation support.
[BLAME] benchmark_1/parts/dag_engine/lib/dag_engine_impl.py: WaveScheduler.initialize() at lines 332-334 sets _states={} but does not call _sync_states() to discover nodes from the DAG, leaving the internal state mapping empty; this causes WaveScheduler.get_state (line 463) and WaveScheduler.get_all_states (line 470) to raise KeyError when queried before next_wave is called, violating the low-level contract GROUNDING that mandates 'Synchronizes dynamic node state by discovering registered nodes from _dag.all_nodes(), initializing root nodes to NodeState.READY and non-root nodes to NodeState.PENDING'; additionally DAGRunner.cancel (lines 658-666) calls scheduler.get_state(nid) without ensuring states are synced, causing KeyError at line 664 when nodes exist in the DAG but not in _states
[BLAME] benchmark_1/parts/dag_engine/tests/dag_engine_impl_test.py: Test suite asserts unmandated behaviors not specified in low/dag_engine_impl.pyi or low/dag_engine.pyi: (1) TestDAGAddNode.test_add_node_duplicate_raises (line 104-110) asserts that add_node raises Exception on duplicate node_id, but the low-level contract for add_node specifies only 'MUST register the node definition into the graph' with no duplicate-checking requirement; (2) TestWaveSchedulerFailures.test_continue_on_error_preserves_independent (line 506-519) and test_fail_fast_cancels_pending (line 479-491) add both A and B to the same wave and call mark_running on both before marking A failed, then assert B is still READY or CANCELLED, but B was already transitioned to RUNNING by the test's own mark_running call, contradicting the assertion; (3) TestWaveSchedulerGetAllStates.test_get_all_states_after_init (line 570-577) and test_get_state_returns_current (line 579-585) query WaveScheduler state immediately after adding nodes without calling next_wave first, asserting that get_state and get_all_states auto-populate states, but the low-level contract only mandates that next_wave and is_finished synchronize states, not get_state or get_all_states.
[CHANGE] benchmark_1/parts/dag_engine/lib/dag_engine_impl.py: Fixed WaveScheduler.initialize() to call _sync_states() for proper node state discovery, and fixed DAGRunner.cancel() to call scheduler.is_finished() (which syncs states) before querying node states, preventing KeyError at runtime.
[CHANGE] benchmark_1/parts/dag_engine/tests/dag_engine_impl_test.py: Resolved all feedback: (1) Removed test_add_node_duplicate_raises which asserted unmandated duplicate-checking behavior not in spec; (2) Fixed test_fail_fast_cancels_pending and test_continue_on_error_preserves_independent to only mark the failing node as RUNNING instead of marking all nodes in the wave, which contradicted subsequent state assertions; (3) Fixed test_get_all_states_after_wave and test_get_state_returns_current to call next_wave() before querying scheduler states, per spec which mandates next_wave synchronizes states.
[BLAME] benchmark_1/parts/dag_engine/lib/dag_engine_impl.py: The CHANGE header indicates the author fixed KeyError by calling scheduler.is_finished() before querying states in DAGRunner.cancel() (lines 657-669), but the implementation still violates the low/dag_engine_impl.pyi contract at line 318-324 which mandates 'Marks unstarted ready and pending nodes as CANCELLED via _scheduler.' Instead, line 669 calls scheduler.mark_failed(nid, FailurePolicy.FAIL_FAST) which per the mark_failed contract (line 239) sets _states[node_id] to NodeState.FAILED, not CANCELLED. The test_cancel test correctly asserts NodeState.CANCELLED but the lib transitions to NodeState.FAILED. The fix should directly mark nodes as CANCELLED via scheduler.set_state or equivalent, not via mark_failed which intentionally sets FAILED state.
[CHANGE] benchmark_1/parts/dag_engine/lib/dag_engine_impl.py: Fixed DAGRunner.cancel() to directly set NodeState.CANCELLED on unstarted nodes via scheduler._states instead of calling mark_failed (which incorrectly sets FAILED). Also cast to concrete WaveScheduler to access internal _sync_states/_lock/_states for thread-safe state transitions per the low-level contract.
